        <p>Understanding meta tags in HTML.</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section>
            <h2>What Are Meta Tags?</h2>
            <p>
                Meta tags provide information about a webpage to
                browsers and search engines. They are placed inside
                the head element of an HTML document.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Important Meta Tags</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Charset: Defines character encoding.</li>
                <li>Viewport: Helps webpages display correctly on mobile devices.</li>
                <li>Description: Summarizes the webpage for search engines.</li>
                <li>Author: Identifies the content author.</li>
                <li>Robots: Gives crawling and indexing instructions to search engines.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Audit Checklist</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Check whether the title is present.</li>
                <li>Check whether the description is meaningful.</li>
                <li>Verify the viewport meta tag.</li>
                <li>Confirm the correct character encoding.</li>
                <li>Ensure all meta tags are inside the head element.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </main>

